 This creates `.venv_data_collection` using Python 3.10 via `uv`. It installs `gear_sonic[data_collection]` which includes `lerobot`, `av`, `opencv-python`, and other required packages. It also installs `espeak` (system package) for voice feedback during recording.
 
+With `--ov`, CPU-only PyTorch is pre-installed from the PyTorch CPU index before the LeRobot resolve, so the CUDA wheels (and their NVIDIA library deps) are skipped — useful when this venv co-exists with `.venv_inference` built via `install_inference.sh --ov`.
