 ### 1. Isaac-GR00T PolicyServer
 
-The PolicyServer runs on a machine with a GPU. It loads your finetuned VLA model
-and serves inference over ZMQ.
+The PolicyServer loads your finetuned VLA model and serves inference over ZMQ.
+It can run on an NVIDIA GPU machine (default PyTorch path) or, with the
+OpenVINO fork, on an Intel CPU / iGPU / NPU.
+
+#### Option A — PyTorch on CUDA (default)
 
 Install [Isaac-GR00T](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Isaac-GR00T) and start the server:
 
@@ -54,6 +57,60 @@ uv run python gr00t/eval/run_gr00t_server.py \
     --port 5550
 ```
 
+#### Option B — OpenVINO on Intel CPU / iGPU / NPU
+
+Use the OpenVINO-enabled Isaac-GR00T fork. The server still loads the
+PyTorch shell briefly on CPU/FP32, then swaps the VLA model for compiled OpenVINO IR
+models that run on `--ov-device`.
+
+`bash install_scripts/install_inference.sh --ov` (covered in the
+[Inference Environment](#2-inference-environment) section below) clones
+the fork's `ov-n1.7` branch automatically. To do it manually:
+
+```bash
+git clone -b ov-n1.7 \
+    https://github.com/intel-sandbox/frameworks.industrial.motion-control.isaac-gr00t.git
+```
+
+The fork ships pre-exported OpenVINO IR files for the released SONIC
+checkpoint under `/path/to/ov_model`. If you don't have your own finetuned
+PyTorch checkpoint yet, point `--model-path` at the public Hugging Face
+release, e.g. `poisonousID/GR00T-N1.7-UNITREE-G1-SONIC-10000` — `gr00t` will
+download it on first run via the `huggingface_hub` cache.
+
+```bash
+# From the OpenVINO-enabled Isaac-GR00T fork
+uv run python gr00t/eval/run_gr00t_server.py \
+    --model-path /path/to/finetuned_model \
+    --embodiment-tag UNITREE_G1_SONIC \
+    --enable-ov \
+    --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_model \
+    --ov-device GPU \
+    --use-fused-dit \
+    --port 5550
+```
+
+`--ov-model-dir` must point to a directory of OpenVINO IR files. FP16, FP16-INT8, and
+FP16-INT4 precisions are auto-detected from the filename suffix. The
+fork's bundled `/path/to/ov_model` directory matches the
+`/path/to/finetuned_model` checkpoint.
+
+OpenVINO server flags:
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `--enable-ov` | `false` | Enable the OpenVINO inference path |
+| `--ov-model-dir` | — | Directory with OpenVINO IR files (required with `--enable-ov`) |
+| `--ov-device` | `GPU` | OpenVINO device: `CPU`, `GPU`, `NPU`, or `AUTO` |
+| `--full-ov` / `--no-full-ov` | `true` | Full OV path vs. ViT-only acceleration (rest stays in PyTorch) |
+| `--use-fused-dit` | `false` | Use the fused DiT IR (`dit_fused_*.xml`) when available |
+| `--force-fp32` | `false` | Force FP32 on the full OV GPU path (workaround for Intel iGPU NaN) |
+
+When `--enable-ov` is set, `--device` is ignored — the PyTorch shell
+always loads on CPU because (a) the OV setup deletes the heavy PyTorch
+submodules right after, and (b) OV inputs are numpy arrays so a CUDA
+shell would only add device-transfer overhead on every call.
+
