 Make sure port 5550 (or your chosen port) is accessible between the two machines.
 
+## Co-Located Server (single Intel box)
+
+The PolicyServer and SONIC stack can run on the same machine — handy when
+prototyping with the OpenVINO fork on a single Intel host:
+
+```bash
+# Terminal A — OV PolicyServer (ov-n1.7 branch of the fork)
+cd /path/to/frameworks.industrial.motion-control.isaac-gr00t
+uv run python gr00t/eval/run_gr00t_server.py \
+    --model-path poisonousID/GR00T-N1.7-UNITREE-G1-SONIC-10000 \
+    --embodiment-tag UNITREE_G1_SONIC \
+    --enable-ov --ov-model-dir /path/to/ov_model --ov-device GPU \
+    --use-fused-dit --port 5550
+
+# Terminal B — SONIC (sim) + VLA client + camera + keyboard
+cd /path/to/GR00T-WholeBodyControl
+python gear_sonic/scripts/launch_inference.py \
+    --sim --no-data-exporter \
+    --policy-host localhost --policy-port 5550 \
+    --prompt "pick up the apple"
+```
+
+`--no-data-exporter` skips the recording pane (and the `.venv_data_collection`
+prerequisite). On a modest box, watch the C++ deploy pane for control-loop
+timing warnings — VLA inference, OV kernels, and the WBC controller all share
+the same host.
+
 ## Latency Compensation
 
 The inference loop automatically compensates for network and compute latency.
